Package: coole
Architecture: any
Multi-Arch: foreign
Depends: ${shlibs:Depends}, ${misc:Depends}
Recommends: coole-lua
Suggests: libx11-6, libaspell15 | libhunspell-1.7-0, universal-ctags
Description: console text editor, a continuation of cooledit
 coole is a console text editor that continues cooledit by Paul Sheer.  It
 has syntax highlighting, code folding, an
 undo history browser, keyboard macros with a macro explorer, ctags and
 etags navigation, spell checking, a user menu, multiple windows, skins and
 editable key bindings.
 .
 Spell checking uses aspell or hunspell, whichever is installed; the
 library is loaded at run time.
 .
 The coole-lua package adds the Lua runtime, which runs editor scripts.

Package: coole-lua
Architecture: any
Depends: ${shlibs:Depends}, ${misc:Depends},
         coole (= ${binary:Version})
Description: Lua runtime and scripts for the coole text editor
 The Lua runtime plugin that coole loads at run time, and the editor
 scripts that come with it, such as inserting the date and time, sorting
 the selection, formatting a paragraph, drawing a table or inserting the
 output of a command.
 .
 Without this package coole runs, and the features written in Lua are
 absent.
